   "notes": [
    "(1) Voltages other than the differential input voltage are measured from ground, taken as the point midway between VCC+ and VCC-.",
    "(2) An input may never go beyond the supply voltage in magnitude, nor beyond 15 V, whichever limit is lower.",
    "(3) A differential voltage is the non-inverting input measured from the inverting input.",
    "(4) A short circuit heats the chip; shorting every amplifier at once can dissipate enough to destroy it.",
    "(5) Tying the output to ground or to either supply rail is allowed; supply voltage and temperature must then be held low enough that the dissipation rating holds.",
    "(6) HBM: 100 pF through 1.5 kΩ, applied between every pair of pins in turn, the remaining pins left open.",
    "(7) MM: 200 pF charged to the rated voltage and dumped straight between two pins with no added resistance (under 5 Ω internal), for every pin pair, the remaining pins left open.",
    "(8) CDM: package and pins together take the rated voltage as one body, then discharge straight to ground."
   ]
