 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Family",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Two independent JFET-input op amps share one package and one pair of supply pins. TL072, TL072A and TL072B differ in input offset voltage: 10, 6 and 3 mV max at 25 °C. An I in the order code is the -40 to +105 °C grade, a C the 0 to +70 °C grade; Y codes are the automotive-grade SO-8 parts."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input stage",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The input stage is built from matched high-voltage JFETs and bipolar transistors on one monolithic die. Input resistance is 10^12 Ω, and bias and offset currents are in picoamps at 25 °C. The input bias currents are junction leakage and about double for each 10 °C of junction temperature."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Input range",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The common-mode range reaches up to the positive supply (-12 V to +15 V typical at ±15 V), and the differential input range is wide (±30 V absolute). No input may exceed the supply voltage in magnitude, nor 15 V."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Output",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "The output is protected against short circuits and can be held shorted to ground or either rail without time limit, provided dissipation stays inside its rating; shorting both outputs at once can overheat the chip. Short-circuit current is 40 mA typical."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Compensation and dynamics",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Frequency compensation is internal. Typical figures at ±15 V: 16 V/µs slew rate, 4 MHz gain-bandwidth, 45° phase margin, 15 nV/√Hz noise at 1 kHz and 0.01 % THD. The part is free of latch-up."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Supply",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Runs from 6 V to 36 V total supply. With no load the supply current is 1.4 mA typical and 2.5 mA max; across temperature, the current per amplifier falls from about 1.76 mA at -75 °C to 1.0 mA at 125 °C."
  }
 ],
